Camera
------

The product has |spec:Camera|. 

Note: I2C address 0x10 is occupied by audio IC, which conflicts with Raspberry Pi Camera V2/V2.1 (Sony IMX219) module. When you select a camera, please choose carefully because not all electrically compatible camera modules have mature software support for the ESP32-P4.

OV5647 uses I2C address 0x36.

.. rst-class:: text-center

   |camera_img|

   *15 pin 1.0mm MIPI-CSI (2-lane) interface*

.. table:: Camera Connector Pin-out
   :align: center
   :width: 100%
   :widths: auto

   +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
   | **Camera Connector Pin Definition:**                                                                          |
   +================+===============================+==============================================================+
   | **Pin Number** | **Definition**                | **Description**                                              |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 1          | GND                           | Power Ground                                                 |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 2          | CAM1_DN0                      | CAM1_DN0                                                     |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 3          | CAM1_DP0                      | CAM1_DP0                                                     |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 4          | GND                           | Power Ground                                                 |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 5          | CAM1_DN1                      | CAM1_DN1                                                     |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 6          | CAM1_DP1                      | CAM1_DP1                                                     |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 7          | GND                           | Power Ground                                                 |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 8          | CAM1_CN                       | CAM1 Clock signal Negative                                   |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 9          | CAM1_CP                       | CAM1 Clock signal Positive                                   |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 10         | GND                           | Power Ground                                                 |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 11         | CAM GPIO                      | Camera enable, pulled up to 3.3V (camera always enabled)     |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 12         | NC                            | Not connected                                                |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 13         | SCL0                          | I2C SCL (GPIO8), shared with on-board I2C devices            |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 14         | SDA0                          | I2C SDA (GPIO7), shared with on-board I2C devices            |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
   | Pin 15         | +3.3V                         | System +3.3V Power Output, No more than 500mA Current output |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+

.. attention::

    #) The camera interface is not mounted by default.
    #) Check the orientation of the ribbon cable (pin 1 / pin 15) carefully, and power off before connecting or removing the camera.

